  "question": {
    "text": "If the coordinates at one end of a diameter of the circle $x^{2}+y^{2}-8 x-4 y+c=0$ are (-3,2) , then the coordinates at the other end are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9RP8j",
      "text": "(5,3)",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5D5ba",
      "text": "(6,2)",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OaDNq",
      "text": "(1,-8)",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "JLTpq",
      "text": "(11,2)",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The centre of the given circle is $\\mathrm{C} \\equiv(4,2)$\r\n\r\nLet $A \\equiv(-3,2)$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/oPn8SV17oF4gRa73rlmL9sWyWstn65noHV_Lechikcs.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nIf $(\\alpha, \\beta)$ are the coordinates of the other end of the diameter, then, as the middle ploint of the diameter is the centre,\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{\\alpha-3}{2}=4$ and $\\frac{\\beta+2}{2}=2 \\Rightarrow \\alpha=11, \\beta=2$\r\n\r\nThus, the coordinates of the other end of diameter are (11,2)",
    "image": null
  },
